From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:09:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accounts: the network service account answers with the
 chain's token

hle_account.c has carried the whole nn::account surface with the real mangled names all along, and
six of its entries were the online cut: EnsureNetworkServiceAccountAvailable,
GetNetworkServiceAccountId, LoadNetworkServiceAccountIdTokenCache,
ShowLicenseRequirementsForNetworkService, IsNetworkServiceAccountAvailable, the async form and
AsyncContext::GetResult. They answer from the dauth chain now, with DM_NEXTENDO on.

The application id is per-game data the launcher already knows, so it comes from DM_NEXTENDO_APP_ID
and with it unset there is no network service account at all - the offline answer, unchanged.

The account id is FNV-1a over the device id: stable between runs, different between installs, which
is what the servers key their data on.

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: it turns six of hle_account.c's "cut" entries into the real network service account, fed by the dauth chain; upstream deliberately ships offline, and the fork keeps this behind DM_NEXTENDO
Issue: none opened yet — this is the seam the Nextendo work was for

